---
title: Caesar cipher
tags: tools
summary: >-
    Shifts every letter a set number of places along the alphabet, wrapping round from Z to A.
---
{% from "macros/tool.njk" import toolSection with context %}
{% from "macros/tool-frame.njk" import toolFrame %}
{% set filename = page.fileSlug %}
{% set intro %}
    <p>A very simple method of encryption, also known as a shift cipher. It shifts the alphabet a set number of spaces, and the letters pushed off the end start again at the beginning.</p>
    <p>The most common Caesar cipher is ROT13, where <code class="tool-example">A</code> becomes <code class="tool-example">N</code>. You can optionally add a key to encrypt your results further. It builds a custom alphabet to shift through: see the <a href="/ciphers/keyword/" class="text-convrtr">Keyword cipher</a> for how a key makes an alphabet.</p>
    <p>More on the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caesar_cipher" class="text-convrtr">Caesar cipher</a> Wikipedia page.</p>
{% endset %}
{% call toolSection(intro) %}
{% call toolFrame(filename, "Caesar cipher", placeholder = "Example: Hello → 5 [shift] → Mjqqt", actions = [{ id: filename + "Run", label: "Shift" }]) %}
{#- One shift at a time: previous and next apply the new shift straight away, as Shift does #}
<div class="tool-field">
    <div class="tool-field__head">
        <label class="tool-field__label" for="{{ filename }}Shift">Shift</label>
        <span class="caesar-map" id="{{ filename }}Map"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="input-group tool-stepper">
        <button class="btn btn-outline-convrtr btn-icon-text" type="button" id="{{ filename }}Prev" aria-label="Previous shift"><i class="bi bi-chevron-left" aria-hidden="true"></i></button>
        <input type="number" class="form-control caesar-shift" id="{{ filename }}Shift" min="1" max="25" value="3" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="{{ filename }}Map {{ filename }}Status">
        <button class="btn btn-outline-convrtr btn-icon-text" type="button" id="{{ filename }}Next" aria-label="Next shift"><i class="bi bi-chevron-right" aria-hidden="true"></i></button>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="tool-field">
    <label class="tool-field__label" for="{{ filename }}Key"><span class="visually-hidden">Caesar cipher </span>Key</label>
    <input type="text" class="form-control caesar-key" id="{{ filename }}Key" placeholder="Optional" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="{{ filename }}Status">
</div>
{% endcall %}
{% endcall %}
